.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KVM-MESH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kvm-mesh
.Nd put running virtual machines, and this host, on a private WireGuard mesh
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm up
.Ar mesh
.Ar subnet
.Ar vm ...
.Nm
.Cm add
.Ar mesh
.Ar vm ...
.Nm
.Cm status
.Ar mesh
.Nm
.Cm down
.Ar mesh
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
joins a set of running machines into a WireGuard mesh: every machine is a
peer of every other, and this host joins too, so it can reach them on the
mesh.
The mesh needs no physical network card; it rides libvirt's bridge.
.Pp
.Cm up ,
in order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
finds each machine's address with
.Xr kldload-vm-ip 8 ;
.It
logs in to it as root over
.Xr ssh 1 ,
makes it a key pair of its own \(em a key baked into a golden would be the
same on every clone, which is not a mesh \(em and brings up an interface
named after the mesh, at
.Ar subnet Ns Pa \&. Ns Ar n ,
the machines taking 1 upward;
.It
gives every machine every other as a peer;
.It
joins this host at
.Ar subnet Ns Pa .254 ;
.It
waits for every peer to complete a handshake, and says how many did.
.El
.Pp
The members, their ids, keys and addresses are recorded in
.Pa /var/lib/kldload/mesh/ Ns Ar mesh Ns Pa .members ,
which
.Xr kldload-estate 8
reads to tell a stopped member from one that left.
The port is derived from the mesh's name, so two meshes on one host do
not collide and a mesh keeps its port when rebuilt.
.Pp
Machines must be running, reachable, accept root's key, and have
.Xr wg 8
installed.
One that is not is skipped with the reason, and the count of those that
joined is printed.
.Pp
.Nm
must run as root; run as a user it re-executes itself with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Fl -help
needs neither.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm up Ar mesh subnet vm ...
Build the mesh, or extend it, across the named machines.
.Ar mesh
is also the interface's name: letters, digits,
.Ql _
and
.Ql - ,
up to 15, starting with a letter or digit.
.Ar subnet
is three octets,
.Ql 10.254.0 ;
the network plan keeps
.Ql 10.254.0.0/16
for these meshes
.Pq Xr kldload-netplan 8 .
.It Cm add Ar mesh vm ...
Join more machines to a mesh that is up.
A machine already in it is joined again with its old id, which refreshes
its configuration.
.It Cm status Ar mesh
The members recorded, this host's address on the mesh, and how many peers
there are and have handshaked.
.It Cm down Ar mesh
Remove the interface from every member it can reach and from this host,
and forget the members.
A member that does not answer loses its interface when it next boots.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KVM_MESH_SSH_KEY
The key root logs in to the machines with; default
.Pa /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/mesh/ Ns Ar mesh Ns Pa .members
One line per member: name, id, public key, address.
.It Pa /etc/wireguard/ Ns Ar mesh Ns Pa .key , .pub , .setconf
In each member: its key pair and interface configuration.
The key is kept, and used again if it joins the same mesh again.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done; for
.Cm up
and
.Cm add ,
every peer handshaked.
.It 1
No machine joined, or not every peer handshaked, or a step failed.
.It 2
A usage error: a missing operand, a name that is not a mesh name, a subnet
that is not three octets, an unknown command.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-29, with two throwaway clones of a
Rocky Linux golden,
.Ql mh-3457638-a
and
.Ql mh-3457638-b ,
deleted afterwards.
