.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written after 2026-09-02, generalised from the meshes
.Xr klab 8
and
.Xr kube-cluster 8
already built for their own machines.
Its first run peered one machine with its neighbours and left two with
none, and exited 0: a child process had read the rest of the loop's
input.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: the script each machine is sent was a
double-quoted string with a comment in it that read
.Ql $(ip link del)
and
.Ql $(link add) ,
so every join ran both on this host, as root, before the script was sent;
a mesh name reached a file path unchecked; and
.Cm down
reported removing an interface from machines it had not reached.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A mesh does not survive a reboot.
The interfaces, on the machines and on this host, are made by hand, not
by a unit, so a machine that restarts comes back off the mesh, and this
host after a reboot has none of its meshes; the members files stay.
Run
.Cm up
again with the same machines: each keeps its key, and, named in the same
order, its id.
.Pp
The machines' host keys are not checked; clones get new ones each time.
